## 7. Database (Prisma)

- Migrations only via Prisma — never alter tables manually
- Every model has `id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`
- Soft deletes via `deletedAt` for business-critical entities
- All foreign keys declared in schema
- Indexes on all FK fields and frequently-queried fields
- No raw SQL unless Prisma cannot express the query

```bash
npx prisma migrate dev --name descriptive_name   # development
npx prisma migrate deploy                         # production
npm run prisma:generate                           # after schema changes
npx prisma db seed                                # seed data
```

Avoid N+1 — use `include` for relations:

```typescript
// Good
const employee = await prisma.employee.findUnique({
    where: { id },
    include: { departments: true, workHistorys: true }
});

// Bad — N+1
const employee = await prisma.employee.findUnique({ where: { id } });
const departments = await prisma.department.findMany({ where: { employeeId: id } });
```

