## 8. Testing Standards

### Coverage threshold: 90% (branches, functions, lines, statements)

### Test file naming and location
```
src/backend/src/domain/models/__tests__/Employee.test.ts
src/backend/src/application/services/__tests__/employeeService.test.ts
src/backend/src/presentation/controllers/__tests__/employeeController.test.ts
```

### Test structure template

```typescript
describe('EmployeeService - createEmployee', () => {
    beforeEach(() => {
        jest.clearAllMocks();
    });

    it('should create employee when all inputs are valid', async () => {
        // Arrange
        const input = { firstName: 'Jane', lastName: 'Doe', email: 'jane@example.com' };
        (Employee.findOneByEmail as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(null);
        const savedEmployee = new Employee({ id: 1, ...input });
        jest.spyOn(Employee.prototype, 'save').mockResolvedValue(savedEmployee);

        // Act
        const result = await createEmployee(input);

        // Assert
        expect(result.email).toBe('jane@example.com');
        expect(Employee.prototype.save).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
    });

    it('should throw ConflictError when email already exists', async () => {
        // Arrange
        (Employee.findOneByEmail as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(new Employee({ id: 1 }));

        // Act & Assert
        await expect(createEmployee({ email: 'jane@example.com' }))
            .rejects.toThrow(ConflictError);
    });
});
```

### Test categories required per function
1. Happy path — valid inputs, expected output
2. Validation errors — missing/invalid fields
3. Not found — entity doesn't exist
4. Conflicts — duplicate data
5. Server errors — DB failure
6. Edge cases — empty arrays, boundary values

### Mocking rules
- Mock all Prisma calls in unit tests
- Mock domain models in service tests
- Mock services in controller tests
- Use `jest.mock()` at file top for module-level mocks
- `jest.clearAllMocks()` in `beforeEach`

### Coverage reports
```bash
npm test                    # run all tests
npm run test:coverage       # with coverage report
# Reports saved to: coverage/YYYYMMDD-backend-coverage.md
```

