## 9. Logging

Use the project logger — never `console.log` in production code:

```typescript
import { logger } from '../infrastructure/logger';

logger.info('Employee created', { employeeId: employee.id });
logger.error('Failed to create employee', { error: error.message, input });
logger.warn('Deprecated endpoint called', { path: req.path });
```

Log levels: `error` (exceptions), `warn` (unexpected but handled), `info` (key events), `debug` (dev only)

---

## 10. Security

- Validate and sanitize all inputs (validator.ts)
- Rate limit all public endpoints
- Never expose stack traces in production responses
- Validate required env vars at startup — fail fast if missing
- CORS configured explicitly — no wildcard `*` in production
- Helmet middleware on all routes
- No SQL injection possible via Prisma parameterization
- Audit log for mutations on sensitive entities (employees, applications)

