## Anti-Patterns

These patterns are **never acceptable**. The AI MUST reject, refactor, or flag them when encountered.

| Pattern | Why | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `any` type in TypeScript | Defeats type safety; runtime errors | Explicit type or `unknown` with narrowing |
| Business logic in route handlers / controllers | Untestable without HTTP setup | Move to application service |
| Prisma calls outside the repository layer | Leaks ORM dependency into business logic | Repository pattern wrapping Prisma |
| `console.log` in production code | No log levels, no structure, leaked in client bundles | `logger.info()` / `logger.error()` |
| Unhandled promise rejections (floating `.then()` / `await` without `try/catch`) | Silent crashes in Node.js | Always `await` with `try/catch` or `.catch()` |
| Cross-domain direct imports (`import { UserRepo } from '../../auth/...'`) | Violates bounded contexts | Expose through interface/service boundary |
| Missing `zod` validation on user input | Type system doesn't protect at runtime | Validate at controller boundary with zod |
